Validation Reference

Validation Objective

Demonstrate that the adaptive decision-generation capability enables the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) to produce appropriate response decisions from interpreted operating contexts in representative operational situations.

---

Validation Method

Validation shall be performed through one or more of the following methods:

Method| Purpose
Operational Evaluation| Assess decision-generation behavior under representative operating conditions.
Scenario-Based Assessment| Evaluate generated decisions across varying, uncertain, and interacting operational situations.
Comparative Assessment| Compare generated decisions against approved operational expectations and applicable decision criteria.
Stakeholder Acceptance| Confirm that the decision-generation capability fulfills its intended role within the adaptive intelligence architecture.

---

Validation Reference

Detailed validation scenarios, operational conditions, decision criteria, acceptance records, and supporting evidence shall be maintained within the AVIA Validation domain and referenced from this objective.

---

Validation Success Criteria

Validation shall demonstrate that the system:

- Generates decisions that are appropriate to representative operating contexts.
- Considers relevant alternatives and applicable constraints.
- Produces decisions that support the intended adaptive behavior of AVIA.
- Maintains appropriate behavior when operating conditions change.
- Represents uncertainty appropriately where decision generation is affected by incomplete or uncertain context.
- Provides decision information suitable for subsequent authorization and execution.
- Fulfills the engineering intent established by SO-F-004.

---

Validation Boundary

Validation of SO-F-004 shall assess whether generated decisions fulfill their intended operational purpose.

It shall not independently establish:

- Whether the decision is legally or operationally authorized.
- Whether a separate authority mechanism has correctly approved the decision.
- Whether the vehicle successfully executes the approved decision.

Those capabilities shall be validated under their respective architectural responsibilities.

---

Authorization Consideration

A generated decision may be considered operationally appropriate without being authorized for execution.

Therefore validation evidence shall preserve the distinction between:

Appropriate Decision
        ≠
Authorized Decision

The authorization architecture shall determine how appropriate generated decisions become approved decisions.

